WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.089 --> 00:00:03.469
Good morning, William; it's Friday, March
4, one of the very few dates that's also a

00:00:03.469 --> 00:00:05.340
sentence... March forth!

00:00:05.340 --> 00:00:09.860
Today, we're gonna take a voyage into the
dark heart of contemporary narcissistic megalomania

00:00:09.860 --> 00:00:12.309
by playing "Sheen or Gaddafi?"!

00:00:12.309 --> 00:00:15.679
The rules are pretty simple, Hank, I'm gonna
tell you a series of quotations and you're

00:00:15.679 --> 00:00:20.360
going to guess whether that quotation was
said by Charlie Sheen or Muammar Gaddafi.

00:00:20.360 --> 00:00:24.140
However, for the purposes of making the game
challenging, I will be translating Muammar

00:00:24.140 --> 00:00:28.660
Gaddafi's quotations from Arabic, because
otherwise it'd be really... easy to figure

00:00:28.660 --> 00:00:33.070
out, you know. "Is it in Arabic?" would be
the primary question you would be asking.

00:00:33.070 --> 00:00:34.140
Okay, let's just play!

00:00:34.140 --> 00:00:40.030
Your first quotation, "Every great movement
begins with one man, and I guess that's me."

00:00:40.030 --> 00:00:43.510
Who said it: Sheen or Gaddafi?

00:00:43.510 --> 00:00:48.250
Time to guess. Just click on whoever you think
said it. By the way, you might wanna turn

00:00:48.250 --> 00:00:53.829
on annotations; I mean, if you're still watching
this video, it's presumably because your annotations

00:00:53.829 --> 00:00:58.199
aren't on. Turn them on! And then click "Sheen"
or "Gaddafi."

